messages:
randall: quick heads-up-- after the remap patch we saw a flake where kvcache returned an old PFN during async remap. minimal log attached. anyone know the remap publish order?

elen: remap currently does: write_new_pfn(); queue_mmu_unmap(old); clear_old_slot(); we did that to reduce writer stalls.

sam: logs show kvcache::read hit the slot between queue_mmu_unmap and clear_old_slot. produced a stale DMA paddr.

miguel: ordering race between MMU notifier and CPU readers. Two options: slow writer (wait for notifier ack) or make reader robust (version/epoch). Writers are on eviction hot path so prefer reader guard.

anya: propose 2-slot epoch on page metadata. bump epoch before/after remap so readers can detect concurrent writers. cheap fastpath, slowpath handles retry/quiesce.

randy: sketch:
```
writer:
  atomic_inc(epoch);
  publish_pfn();
  smp_wmb();
  atomic_inc(epoch);

reader:
  pre = read_atomic(epoch);
  smp_rmb();
  pfn = read_pfn();
  smp_rmb();
  post = read_atomic(epoch);
  if (pre != post) goto slowpath;
```
slowpath: spin for X us then wait for notifier or fallback to safe copy.

miguel: spin->escalate seems reasonable. need to pick spin window (10-100us) and measure tail behavior. also watch multi-writer epoch wrap (64-bit epoch solves that).

sam: I'll prototype the epoch fastpath + CI toggles. will add a notifier-delay fault injector and a microbench to measure hotpath overhead.

anya: add telemetry: per-page epoch_retries and global histogram so SRE can alert on spikes. also add unit test that injects delayed notifier to ensure slowpath triggers.

offload-bot: CI: run/host-remap-smoke (gpu-48g) flaked 2/60 runs in last 24h category=mmu-notifier-delay. link: https://ci.redwood.internal/xyz

sam: opened DRAFT PR: kvcache-epoch-guard with tests + injector. tagging reviewers.

randall: solid plan. follow-ups: perf run for spin window, RFC note about long-term writer-quiesce invariant, and telemetry dashboards. thanks all. :thumbsup:
